  "turn_number": 9,
  "player_text": "He is done with me. I step back from the captain and read the notice board, starting with the curfew, so I know whether I can even wait out here.",
  "visible_motivation": "The captain refused a fixed toll and said I will not be let through without business or favor. I need the posted curfew before I decide whether to wait outside.",
  "intended_meaning": "Read the curfew posting on the notice board after being refused passage.",
  "generated_candidate": "You step back from the guard captain, whose imposing silence leaves no room for further coaxing. Your gaze shifts to the weathered notice board pinned firmly to a nearby post. It details the current curfew hours, specifying that all non-essential traffic must clear the gate district by dusk sharp—less than three hours away under the slate-gray sky. The board also lists recent tax schedules, reminding travelers of the shifting tolls depending on goods and origin, though no fixed amount is posted for the day. A warning stands prominently beneath: a local patrol has gone missing northwest of here, its last known route traced past the muddy crate stacks by the northwest mud track. The crowded gate district buzzes with muttered concerns about the patrol’s fate and growing delays caused by the Ash Compact’s increased census and tightened caravan checkpoints.",
